A dilation centered at the origin with a scale factor of $-3$ will multiply each coordinate of a point by $-3$.
So the matrix that represents this dilation is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} -3 & 0 \\ 0 & -3 \end{pmatrix}}$.
The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}-3&0\0&-3\end{pmatrix}

